wn":0.01175,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.333,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":33.3,"pf":[],"description_full":"Alamo Group Inc. manufactures and sells industrial and vegetation management equipment for governmental, industrial, and agricultural uses worldwide. It operates in two segments, Vegetation Management and Industrial Equipment. The Vegetation Management segment offers tractor powered equipment such as rotary, finishing, flail, and disc mowers; rotary cutters; front end loaders, backhoes, tillers, posthole diggers, scraper blades, cultivators, subsoilers, and other tractor attachments and implements. This segment also provides commercial and residential zero turn mowers; hydraulic and mechanical boom and reach mowers; hedge and hedgerow cutters; industrial grass mowers; seedbed preparation equipment; and forestry and tree care tools, including chippers, stump grinders, mulchers, brush cutters, flails, and debarkers, as well as remote control mowers and related replacement parts. Its Industrial Equipment segment offers hydraulic telescoping booms; catch basin and roadway debris vacuum systems; sewer cleaners; vacuum trucks, combination sewer cleaners, hydro excavators, trenchers, and high pressure cleaning systems; truck mounted snow plows, blowers, dump bodies, spreaders, deicers, brine sprayers, snow throwers, and wing systems; salt spreaders; street sweepers, including mechanical broom and regenerative air models; leaf and debris collection equipment and replacement brooms; solid waste and recycling equipment; municipal tractors and attachments; asphalt patchers; underground construction forms; traffic control and crash attenuator trucks; industrial vacuum excavation units; trailer mounted and custom truck mounted systems; and related accessories and truck up fitting services. The company serves the infrastructure building and maintenance, industrial construction, public works, land maintenance, agriculture, and tree care markets. Alamo Group Inc. was founded in 1955 and is headquartered in Seguin, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert P. Hureau | President, CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $982,596 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $422K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $39K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Alamo Group, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.8B market cap on $1.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 25% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $147M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.71\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 10.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.9%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.025280628168655447},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 12% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Valued at a 21% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","32 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Alamo Group (ALG) Stock Is Up 5.0% Today Without Company News","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/alamo-group-alg-stock-5-154515486.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795794315.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(ALG) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/24/ALG_Movement_as_an_Input_in_Quant_Signal_Sets_111926070402_1795133042.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795133042.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Alamo Group (NYSE:ALG) Hits New 52-Week Low \u2013 Time to Sell?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"